":"அவன்","parts":[{"text":"அவன்","lemma":"அவன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"},{"surface":"தாளே","parts":[{"text":"தாள்","lemma":"தாள்","gloss":"feet"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"feet indeed"}]}],"literal":"O bard of the small lute with sweet-toned strings! / Like a turtle living in a pond pierced with a skewer, / O mendicant who, with a large drum of clear drumhead fastened with a fine stick, / does not cease asking, saying, 'Let me see sweet things here, let me rest here!' / O wise-mouthed mendicant! / Like the cool pond in the month of Thai, / in the wide mansion with food that does not decrease however much is taken, / which knows no burning fire other than the cooking fire, / the king of the good country that produces the great medicine (rice), / thinking of the good fame of Killi Valavan, / where the six-legged bee with a sense of smell / hums nearby the small white water lily, / in the small settlement of Pannan of generous-handed giving, / with the sweet-smiling dancer whose hair is fragrant with trumpet flowers / and who has a bright forehead, walking gently, / if you go, you will indeed become prosperous. / His giving is not like an accidental find of gold / by people carrying firewood. / Do not think twice; may his feet live long!","translation":"O bard of the small lute with sweet-toned strings! O wise-mouthed mendicant who, carrying a large drum with a clear drumhead that looks like a pond-turtle pierced with a skewer, never ceases to ask, saying, 'Let me see sweet things here, let me rest here!' If you go, walking gently with your sweet-smiling dancer whose hair is fragrant with trumpet flowers and who has a bright forehead, to the small settlement of the generous Pannan—where the six-legged bees with their keen sense of smell hum near the small white water lilies—and then think of the great fame of Killi Valavan, the king of the fertile country where food is as inexhaustible as a cool pond in winter, and which knows no fire other than the cooking fire, you will indeed prosper. His giving is not like a poor firewood-gatherer accidentally finding gold. Do not hesitate; may his feet live long!","modern":"இனிய இசையையுடைய சிறிய யாழை ஏந்திய பாணனே! குளத்தில் வாழும் ஆமை கம்பியால் குத்தப்பட்டது போன்ற, தெளிந்த தோலையுடைய பெரிய கிணைப் பறையை நல்ல குச்சியால் கட்டி வாசித்துக் கொண்டு, 'இங்கே நல்லவற்றைக் காண்பேனாக, இங்கே தங்கி இளைப்பாறுவேனாக' என்று இடைவிடாது கேட்கும் அறிவுடைய இரவலனே! தை மாதத்துக் குளிர்ந்த குளத்தைப் போல, மக்கள் உண்ண உண்ணக் குறையாத உணவையுடைய அகன்ற அரண்மனையில், சமையல் நெருப்பைத் தவிர நாட்டைச் சுட்டெரிக்கும் பகைவரின் நெருப்பை அறியாத, பசியைப் போக்கும் சிறந்த மருந்தாகிய நெல்லை விளைவிக்கும் நல்ல நாட்டின் தலைவனாகிய சோழன் குளமுற்றத்துத் துஞ்சிய கிள்ளி வளவனின் நல்ல புகழை நினைத்துக் கொண்டு, நறுமணத்தை நுகரும் வண்டுகள் சிறிய வெள்ளாம்பல் மலரின் அருகே மொய்த்து ஒலிக்கும், கைகொடுத்து உதவும் வள்ளல் தன்மையுடைய பண்ணனின் சிறுகுடியில், பாதிரிப் பூவின் மணம் கமழும் கூந்தலையும் ஒளிரும் நெற்றியையும் இனிய புன்னகையையும் உடைய விறலியோடு மெல்ல நடந்து செல்வாயானால், நீ வறுமை நீங்கிச் செல்வம் உடையவன் ஆவாய். அவனுடைய கொடை என்பது விறகு சுமக்கும் ஏழைகள் வழியில் தற்செயலாகப் பொன்னைக் கண்டெடுத்தது போன்ற தற்செயலான நிகழ்வு அன்று. எனவே, ஐயப்படாமல் செல்வாயாக! அவன் திருவடிகள் வாழ்க!","explanation":"This poem is a Paaṇāṟṟuppaṭai (guiding a bard to a patron) in the Purattinai of Paataan, composed by Kovur Kizhar in praise of the Chola king Killi Valavan. The poet addresses a wandering bard who is traveling with his family, including a dancer (virali). He describes the bard's drum, comparing its clear drumhead to a turtle pierced with a skewer. The poet advises the bard to visit the small settlement of Pannan, a generous patron, on his way to the great Chola king Killi Valavan. He assures the bard that the king's generosity is constant and reliable, unlike a poor firewood-gatherer accidentally finding gold. The imagery of the fertile Chola country, where the only fire known is the cooking fire and food is as inexhaustible as a cool pond in winter, highlights the peace and prosperity under the king's rule.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.1,0.7],[0.7,1.12],[1.25,1.62],[1.62,1.88],[2.0,2.6],[2.6,2.7],[2.7,2.9],[2.9,2.9],[2.9,2.9],[2.9,5.0],[5.0,5.2],[5.2,5.7],[5.7,6.1],[6.1,7.2],[7.2,7.5],[7.5,7.9],[7.9,8.0],[8.0,8.4],[8.4,8.9],[8.9,10.0],[10.0,10.2],[10.2,10.3],[10.3,11.1],[11.1,11.7],[11.7,12.2],[12.2,12.2],[12.2,13.1],[13.1,14.1],[14.1,14.8],[14.8,15.0],[15.0,15.2],[15.2,15.87],[16.2,16.6],[16.6,16.82],[16.9,17.5],[18.2,19.0],[19.0,19.3],[19.3,19.5],[19.5,20.2],[20.2,21.1],[21.1,21.3],[21.3,21.6],[21.74,22.3],[22.3,23.2],[23.2,23.2],[23.2,23.7],[23.7,24.0],[24.0,24.93],[24.93,24.93],[24.93,25.11],[25.11,25.3],[25.3,26.05],[26.05,26.05],[26.05,27.3],[27.3,28.4],[28.4,29.4],[29.4,29.5],[29.5,29.8],[29.8,30.1],[30.1,31.0],[31.0,31.6],[31.6,32.0],[32.0,32.2],[32.2,33.7],[33.7,34.0],[34.0,34.1],[34.1,34.7],[35.68,36.28],[36.28,36.68],[36.68,37.18],[37.28,37.58],[37.58,38.18],[38.18,38.28],[38.28,38.88],[38.88,38.98],[38.98,40.08],[40.08,40.38],[40.38,40.48],[40.48,40.98],[40.98,41.28]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.5],[1.59,1.84],[1.84,2.01],[2.1,2.7],[2.7,2.8],[2.8,3.0],[3.0,3.89],[3.89,4.1],[4.1,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,5.8],[5.8,6.3],[6.3,7.5],[7.5,7.9],[7.9,8.2],[8.2,8.4],[8.4,8.8],[8.8,9.3],[9.3,10.8],[10.8,11.1],[11.1,11.2],[11.2,12.2],[12.2,12.9],[12.9,13.5],[13.5,13.6],[13.6,14.6],[14.6,15.9],[15.9,16.7],[16.7,16.9],[16.9,17.3],[17.3,18.03],[18.4,19.0],[19.0,19.42],[19.5,20.0],[20.84,21.74],[21.74,22.14],[22.14,22.24],[22.24,23.04],[23.04,23.94],[23.94,24.14],[24.14,24.44],[24.62,25.34],[25.34,26.14],[26.14,26.24],[26.24,26.94],[26.94,27.24],[27.24,28.41],[28.41,28.64],[28.64,29.11],[29.34,29.81],[29.81,30.04],[30.04,31.44],[31.44,31.64],[31.64,31.84],[31.84,33.34],[33.34,33.54],[33.54,33.84],[33.84,34.24],[34.24,35.41],[35.41,35.75],[35.87,36.46],[36.8,37.04],[37.04,38.24],[38.24,38.54],[38.54,38.84],[38.84,39.14],[40.2,40.8],[40.9,41.3],[41.3,41.84],[41.84,42.2],[42.2,43.1],[43.